 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Sadly, yes. Spending time looking at small screen leaves your eyes feeling dry and worn. We call it digital eye strain. It is. Want to try something? Blinking every two minutes helps. So does taking short breaks every twenty minutes. You can dim it slightly. A few less brightness levels don't cut down the life of the battery too much. If you find yourself blinking fewer than twenty times a minute, they' worth trying. A clear lens that blocks a lot of high energy blue light can make a big difference.",
